  "body": {
    "id": "prop:two-by-two-reduction",
    "kind": "proposition",
    "statement": "For \\(M=M_0\\), \\(M_0^{+}=\\begin{pmatrix}2&-1\\\\-1&1\\end{pmatrix}\\), so \\(G_1=H_1^2/H_2\\) and \\(G_2=H_2/H_1\\) on \\((0,1]^p\\).",
    "free_symbols": [
      "composition",
      "fixed-composition",
      "pseudoinverse",
      "component-pgf",
      "pooled-pgf",
      "dimension-genes"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:recovery-map",
      "thm:rank-frontier",
      "def:fixed-protocol"
    ],
    "justification": "This checks the general inverse against the smallest genuinely mixed full-rank design.",
    "gap": "The calculation is a sanity reduction and is not presented as a novelty claim.",
    "consumer": "It provides an auditable population inverse for the synthetic two-type application.",
    "proof_tex": "The fixed matrix has determinant \\(1\\), so it is invertible and its Moore--Penrose inverse is its ordinary inverse:\n\\[\nM_0^+=M_0^{-1}\n=\\begin{pmatrix}2&-1\\\\-1&1\\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\nThe rank-frontier identity gives\n\\[\n\\begin{pmatrix}\\log G_1\\\\ \\log G_2\\end{pmatrix}\n=\\begin{pmatrix}2&-1\\\\-1&1\\end{pmatrix}\n\\begin{pmatrix}\\log H_1\\\\ \\log H_2\\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\nAll PGFs are strictly positive on \\((0,1]^p\\), so exponentiation and ordinary division are valid and yield\n\\[\nG_1=\\frac{H_1^2}{H_2},\\qquad G_2=\\frac{H_2}{H_1}.\n\\]",
